WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
It's not easy being a plant.

2
00:00:02.841 --> 00:00:07.841
Plants are often on the dinner menu for hungry animals and insects.

3
00:00:07.842 --> 00:00:10.721
Reproducing can be a challenge.

4
00:00:10.722 --> 00:00:14.650
Sometimes there aren't enough nutrients in the soil for plants to eat.

5
00:00:14.651 --> 00:00:19.144
So how have plants survived?

6
00:00:19.145 --> 00:00:20.591
They've adapted!

7
00:00:20.592 --> 00:00:25.080
Over millions of years, they've found unique ways to survive.

8
00:00:25.081 --> 00:00:29.267
Plants can't run from insects or other animals that are trying to eat them.

9
00:00:29.268 --> 00:00:32.362
But some plants can hide.

10
00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:35.991
They don't jump behind trees or scurry under rocks.

11
00:00:35.992 --> 00:00:39.766
Instead they use camouflage to hide from predators.

12
00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:45.221
These plants have a natural shape or color that helps them blend in with their surroundings.

13
00:00:45.222 --> 00:00:51.055
The Lithops plant has an amazing way to hide itself—it looks like stones!

14
00:00:51.056 --> 00:00:55.607
These plants can be found in southern Africa where it is very dry.

15
00:00:55.608 --> 00:00:58.063
Lithops is a succulent.

16
00:00:58.064 --> 00:01:02.483
Succulents are plants with thick leaves that can store a lot of water. Cactuses

17
00:01:02.484 --> 00:01:06.129
and aloe plants are also succulents. Succulents

18
00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:10.572
usually live in deserts, where water is scarce. During

19
00:01:10.573 --> 00:01:15.310
the rainy season, Lithops ' leaves push up from the soil.

20
00:01:15.311 --> 00:01:20.237
They soak up lots of water and become round like stones.

21
00:01:20.238 --> 00:01:26.509
Since the leaves look like rocks, animals leave them alone, letting them hide in plain sight!

22
00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:30.086
Lithops ' leaves have a small slit on

23
00:01:30.087 --> 00:01:33.786
top. When blooms appear, they grow from the

24
00:01:33.787 --> 00:01:38.073
slit. It looks just like the blooms are growing between two

25
00:01:38.074 --> 00:01:40.302
stones. Some plants don't try to

26
00:01:40.303 --> 00:01:44.924
hide. The titan arum is too big to use camouflage to blend

27
00:01:44.925 --> 00:01:48.557
in. Its blooms are usually about two-and-a-half meters

28
00:01:48.558 --> 00:01:53.191
tall. That makes it one of the largest flowers in the

29
00:01:53.192 --> 00:01:58.583
world. This plant has a special adaptation to help it with reproduction: it

30
00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:04.354
stinks! The titan arum's enormous blossoms smell like dung or rotting

31
00:02:04.355 --> 00:02:09.225
flesh. This is really gross to humans, but it's not gross to

32
00:02:09.226 --> 00:02:14.791
flies. Titan arum plants live in Indonesia's warm, wet

33
00:02:14.792 --> 00:02:18.925
rainforests. When it blooms, the stems of the plant grow

34
00:02:18.926 --> 00:02:22.581
warm. That helps spread its smell far and

35
00:02:22.582 --> 00:02:27.132
wide. When flies smell the blossoms, they come and walk on the

36
00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:29.928
flowers. Bits of pollen stick to their

37
00:02:29.929 --> 00:02:37.330
legs. Then the flies travel to other titan arum flowers, spreading the pollen and helping the titan arum

38
00:02:37.331 --> 00:02:45.223
reproduce. Even though the plant blooms only once every few years, this stinky adaptation is key to the species'

39
00:02:45.224 --> 00:02:48.728
survival. Like humans, plants need to eat to

40
00:02:48.729 --> 00:02:52.111
survive. Most plants simply get their nutrients from

41
00:02:52.112 --> 00:02:57.533
soil. But soil in environments like swamps and marshes has few

42
00:02:57.534 --> 00:03:02.306
nutrients. So certain plants that live in these environments have become

43
00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:04.735
carnivores. That's right—they eat

44
00:03:04.736 --> 00:03:10.255
meat! Some carnivorous plants have sticky leaves that trap insects that land on them.

45
00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:13.325
Others have slippery leaves.

46
00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:18.735
Insects slide down the leaves into a pool of the plants' digestive juices.

47
00:03:18.736 --> 00:03:25.768
Usually carnivorous plants eat insects, but sometimes they eat small frogs or mammals.

48
00:03:25.769 --> 00:03:30.627
Venus flytraps are probably the most well-known carnivorous plants.

49
00:03:30.628 --> 00:03:34.486
They live in the swamps of the southeastern United States.

50
00:03:34.487 --> 00:03:38.240
They have pairs of leaves with small hairs on them.

51
00:03:38.241 --> 00:03:44.433
When an insect touches these hairs, the two leaves snap shut, trapping the insect inside.

52
00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:47.582
Then the plant digests the insect.

53
00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:51.576
This can take a flytrap a week or longer.

54
00:03:51.577 --> 00:03:55.676
But eventually it gets the nutrients it needs.

55
00:03:55.677 --> 00:04:01.845
Staying safe, reproducing, and getting enough nutrients can be challenging for plants.

56
00:04:01.846 --> 00:04:06.101
But plants are tough and have adapted to survive.

57
00:04:06.102 --> 00:04:12.072
The next time you see a plant, take a look and see how it has adapted to its environment.

58
00:04:12.073 --> 00:04:16.702
You might find something pretty cool—or weird!

